{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20","id":1471598,"title":"Hunters Hunted II, Kinfolk, and Ghost Hunters are not Sorcerer 20!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-01T09:15:40-08:00","id":1471598,"title":"Hunters Hunted II, Kinfolk, and Ghost Hunters are not Sorcerer 20!","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Seriously, I am tired of WOD groups treating the HH II, Kinfolk: A Breed Apart, and Ghost Hunter numina as some sort of 20th update for sorcery and psychic powers. The numina that appears in that book, save for True Faith, should be not be seen as some sanctioned update for sorcery or numina given it is weaker and mechanically not the same. These users should be best seen as &quot;dabblers&quot; in numina who only use their power to hunt vampires and other horrible things in the night. They do not have the same mindset as a sorcerer who has the <i>yearning</i> and concerned with their own mystical objectives/enlightenment. The only exception is the Arcanum as they can be considered a proper sorcerous society with them capable of producing Master and Legendary Alchemists but even they tend to treat the other paths as more scholarly subjects.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I understand it may seem simpler to use these numina when trying to run a 20th game, but I honestly feel it would cause more confusion and make psychics and sorcerers weaker and not able to keep up. It is not that hard to convert Sorcerer:Revised over to 20th and I have done it before without much difficulty.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T10:19:54-08:00","id":1471602,"title":"","content":"Agreed. I would also point you to <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/347222\" target=\"_blank\"> Sorcerer: Paths of Power</a>, a Storyteller's Vault product written by <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Charles%20Siegel\" target=\"_blank\">Charles Siegel</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T10:28:40-08:00","id":1471604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471602#post1471602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. I would also point you to <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/347222\" target=\"_blank\"> Sorcerer: Paths of Power</a>, a Storyteller's Vault product written by <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Charles%20Siegel\" target=\"_blank\">Charles Siegel</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have this and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/259124/Sorcerers-Companion\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer's Companion</a>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T11:43:32-08:00","id":1471608,"title":"","content":"I understand the idea, and could like it ... but the thing is: They kinda are, in a way.<br /> <br /> The thing about Numina it's that it's all over the place. And it just happens that sorcery as presented in <i>previous </i>books it's also - as you could say - weaker and mechanically not the same ... <b>AND </b>Sorcerer: Revised was kind of a Revised update for that kind of power.<br /> <br /> I don't remember Sorcerer: Revised stating that sorcerers were supposed to be a splat with powers distinct from the sorcerers presented in <i>previous </i>books. That Paths and Paths aren't the same thing, so to speak - which would make an important distinction to make considering previous books have Paths and sorcerers. On the contrary. I would say it's strongly implied that these sorcerers and those presented in Ascencions Rigth Hand are the same (with updated rules) - since the book does have a section about Sorcerers in the Traditions<br /> <br /> I totally see how you could say they're their own splat now ... but I think it's a bit wrong to say that's &quot;the canon&quot; and the storytellers presenting sorcerers with HH2 rules are *wrong*, when Sorcerer itself doesn't say that the previous Paths of other books (weaker or different as they could be) *aren't* sorcery as defined by the book (thus strongly implying that they *are*).<br /> <br /> I would need to be convinced that that Sorcerer: Revised introduced a completely new splat into WoD, with it's own set of powers (that have the same name for some reason), to believe that they *aren't* the same<br /> <br /> A different thing would be to <i>propose</i> this for M20 - since Sorcerers weren't really updated in the canon, and would make sense with other material - That I would 100% agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-01-2022, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T12:16:48-08:00","id":1471611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471608#post1471608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand the idea, and could like it ... but the thing is: They kinda are, in a way.<br /> <br /> The thing about Numina it's that it's all over the place. And it just happens that sorcery as presented in <i>previous </i>books it's also - as you could say - weaker and mechanically not the same ... <b>AND </b>Sorcerer: Revised was kind of a Revised update for that kind of power.<br /> <br /> I don't remember Sorcerer: Revised stating that sorcerers were supposed to be a splat with powers distinct from the sorcerers presented in <i>previous </i>books. That Paths and Paths aren't the same thing, so to speak - which would make an important distinction to make considering previous books have Paths and sorcerers. On the contrary. I would say it's strongly implied that these sorcerers and those presented in Ascencions Rigth Hand are the same (with updated rules) - since the book does have a section about Sorcerers in the Traditions<br /> <br /> I totally see how you could say they're their own splat now ... but I think it's a bit wrong to say that's &quot;the canon&quot; and the storytellers presenting sorcerers with HH2 rules are *wrong*, when Sorcerer itself doesn't say that the previous Paths of other books (weaker or different as they could be) *aren't* sorcery as defined by the book (thus strongly implying that they *are*).<br /> <br /> I would need to be convinced that that Sorcerer: Revised introduced a completely new splat into WoD, with it's own set of powers (that have the same name for some reason), to believe that they *aren't* the same<br /> <br /> A different thing would be to <i>propose</i> this for M20 - since Sorcerers weren't really updated in the canon, and would make sense with other material - That I would 100% agree.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think from a canon perspective, there has to be some sort of distinction between the two. There are individuals known as &quot;dabblers&quot; in numina that have been mentioned in various WOD sources. We also have to explain what caused sorcery to become more diverse and powerful from the old days of Acensions Right Hand where the magic practices was explicitly stated to be a weaker and inferior power that was not truly magic at all. But by the time of Second editions WOD: Sorcerer, this was changed to the sorcery being real magic just inferior magic and when Sorcerer:Revised was released sorcery just followed a &quot;separate but equal&quot; approach with sorcerers viewed as mages in their own right, just using a different type of magic. We also have to account for the vast difference in how the magic in first edition numina operates and how it functioned in Second edition and Revised. Even the numina that appears in HH II and others are either weaker or different from the numina elsewhere.<br /> <br /> There is also the lore that states the mindset of people who practice sorcery and that lore does not appear for a mortal in HH II, Kinfolk, or Ghost Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T12:38:27-08:00","id":1471614,"title":"","content":"In the context of M20: HH2, Kinfolk, and Ghost Hunter hedge magicians are implicitly Practicing some form of Gutter Magic \u2014 though the HH2 crowd tends to combine this with High Ritual Magic while Kinfolk tend to lean more toward a mix with Shamanism. As Starcomet points out, the flavor text for the Sorcerer books is quite different from the flavor text for most other books featuring Hedge Magic, as the former portrays sorcerers as people who know what they're doing whole the latter portrays hedge magicians as people groping around in the dark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T14:04:32-08:00","id":1471616,"title":"","content":"Since the community, rather than the contents, seem to be a big sticking point here, I think it's worth getting something out of the way:<br /> <br /> A lot of people don't like using the ST Vault because they are of an &quot;official book only&quot; default mindset. The late 90s/early 00s WoD fansites were full of really poorly considered material (before even getting into subjective thoughts like how well written it was, the mechanical merits, and all that). The 00s brought us the OGL boom where d20 got flooded with third party content and even for D&amp;D it was hard to find a good trustworthy aggregator of reviews about all of it to know what was worth looking into and what was safe to skip. The ST Vault is still no promise of quality control, and while the cream of the crop has a lot of word of mouth on places like this, a lot of people aren't active members of the Onyx Path social media platforms, and that leaves a lot of books on there a gamble.<br /> <br /> Secondly, a lot of people feel like the 20th editions are basically over with a few straggler books making it through the works before Paradox finally stops any new official books from getting made. On top of this, sorcerers do not seem to be a high priority for the M20 team (G&amp;M seems to indicate this), nor have we heard of a less Mage oriented direct update to WoD: Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> That means a simple truth: HHII, K:ABA, and WoD: GH are the closest we're probably going to see to an update to the Numina rules for 20th edition books. I would personally take anyone treating them as an update as implicitly meaning, &quot;the best update we're going to get, and the only ones we currently have.&quot;<br /> <br /> I could go into a whole debate about the contents of Sorcerer Revised regarding the attitude around whether or not it is meant to reflect an in-universe distinction between Numina users, or if it was a book meant to boost all Numina users to be more fun in both Numina only play to be more capable, and in mixed splat play to not feel overshadowed. But I don't think it would really mollify the core complaint I'm hearing, since that's not about the contents of the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T14:35:07-08:00","id":1471620,"title":"","content":"The numina that appears in HHII, K:ABA, and WoD: GH, work respectively well for the gamelines they are meant to be in. The numina in HHII, while weaker than the ones in Sorcerer: Revised, it is still useful for a mortal hunter game involving fighting vampires or other creatures. Same with the kinfolk numina and helping a group of Garou fight Pentex or a nest of banes. But for a M20 game that includes sorcerers, they would fall terribly behind their Mage comrades and not be useful at all. And these numina do not even translate well for a Extraordinary Citizen of the technocracy so you can forget about even playing one in a technocracy game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T16:12:57-08:00","id":1471628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471616#post1471616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That means a simple truth: HHII, K:ABA, and WoD: GH are the closest we're probably going to see to an update to the Numina rules for 20th edition books. I would personally take anyone treating them as an update as implicitly meaning, &quot;the best update we're going to get, and the only ones we currently have.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Just a small nitpick: as much as you've pointed out that people don't trust Storyteller's Vault, it <i>is</i> still there. I acknowledge that things like Sorcerer: Paths of Power aren't officially endorsed. But it <i>is</i> a thing, and it's a top seller too, with positive ratings and solid reviews. <br /> <br /> There <i>are</i> more options or there than just HHII, K:ABA, and WoD:GH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-01-2022, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T16:50:49-08:00","id":1471630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471620#post1471620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for a M20 game that includes sorcerers, they would fall terribly behind their Mage comrades and not be useful at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the long run... so did the Sorcerer Revised ones. The XP costs of Numina, plus needing to raise Attributes and Abilities for activation rolls, and getting rituals... it's just too much compared to what a full mage will get out of the XP over time.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer Revised lets you running sorcerers and mages together for a while by increasing their starting level. But the expanded system for Paths didn't really hold up to Spheres over time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471628#post1471628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just a small nitpick:</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a nitpick, it's trying to deny the reality of what people are dealing with.<br /> <br /> How many people that Starcomet is complain about do you really think even know the ST Vault exists, let alone that there's a while quality third party Sorcerer update for 20th in it, let alone are in a group that uses third party material?<br /> <br /> A theoretical option that you never know about, or can't use, isn't a real option for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T17:03:33-08:00","id":1471633,"title":"","content":"And the solution to that is to tell them about Storyteller's Vault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T17:23:19-08:00","id":1471634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471630#post1471630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the long run... so did the Sorcerer Revised ones. The XP costs of Numina, plus needing to raise Attributes and Abilities for activation rolls, and getting rituals... it's just too much compared to what a full mage will get out of the XP over time.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer Revised lets you running sorcerers and mages together for a while by increasing their starting level. But the expanded system for Paths didn't really hold up to Spheres over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this depends somewhat on how much XP the ST plans to give out during their campaign and how focused the sorcerer is in terms of paths. But in general it is true that sorcerers need more XP and time to master their magic compared to a mage and this fits well with the theme of sorcery being more slow, subtle, and studious. There is however a lot of overlap of attributes and abilities for paths and rituals that can save in needing to spend so much XP; like esoterica or occult can be used for <i>several</i> different paths. My sorcerer in a previous mage game used his esoterica and academics for all of his rituals and he used a mix of intelligence, manipulation, and stamina. Increasing those attributes and abilities is not that XP expensive. Rituals only cost 3 XP and making your own is free just very time consuming.<br /> <br /> Also, the Library background can also be used in reducing the amount of XP needed to learn new paths which is more XP savings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T23:28:54-08:00","id":1471646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471633#post1471633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the solution to that is to tell them about Storyteller's Vault.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really? It's not a bad thing to do if someone expresses interest in it, but my whole point here is that getting annoyed at people for acknowledging the reality of their situation is solved by being more empathetic to them; I don't know anybody that's happy that it doesn't look like we're no getting Sorcerer20 except for grognard types that hated Socerer20 for being too big of a departure for WoD:Sorcerer and don't want that repeated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471634#post1471634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in general it is true that sorcerers need more XP and time to master their magic compared to a mage...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. So I don't get the argument that a proper Sorcerer 20th is necessary to make psychics and sorcerers that aren't going to fall behind the mages if that was never actually true in a general sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T00:14:21-08:00","id":1471649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471646#post1471646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really? It's not a bad thing to do if someone expresses interest in it, but my whole point here is that getting annoyed at people for acknowledging the reality of their situation is solved by being more empathetic to them;</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's getting annoyed? Not me. If someone laments the fact that the options they have for X20 Path Magic are HHII, K:ABA, WoD:GH, and nothing else, then they're factually wrong, and I'll point out that they also have S:PoP available to them. If they choose not to use it, that no skin off <i>my</i> nose; and if they continue to pretend that Storyteller's Vault doesn't exist after I've pointed out that it does, <i>they're</i> the ones not acknowledging the reality of their situation, not me. And again, that doesn't affect me in the slightest; so why would I be annoyed?<br /> <br /> This isn't an issue of annoyance or empathy; it's a matter of facts. <br /> <br /> Though I'm beginning to get the impression that I somehow walked into the middle of a conversation, rather than getting in on the ground floor. Is this thread a spinoff of some other thread that I'm unaware of? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471646#post1471646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know anybody that's happy that it doesn't look like we're no getting Sorcerer20 except for grognard types that hated Socerer20 for being too big of a departure for WoD:Sorcerer and don't want that repeated.</div> </div> </div> </div>(I'm assuming you meant SRev instead of the second S20.) My point here is that they're only \u201cnot getting an S20\u201d if they don't accept S:PoP as a proper S20. And like I said, it's no skin off <i>my</i> nose if they don't. But the option <i>is</i> there; and ignorance or denial of it doesn't change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T04:04:40-08:00","id":1471653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471649#post1471649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's getting annoyed? Not me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starcomet's opening post is about being tired of people that treat the official 20th books with Numina in them as the updates to the Numina Paths for the 20th books; I don't see a problem characterizing that as a statement of annoyance.<br /> <br /> You agreed with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone laments... </div> </div> </div>Don't shift the goal posts. The thread started about complaining about other people in the fandom (again, a post you agreed with), not anyone lamenting the available official options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> then they're factually wrong </div> </div> </div>Please explain what a player who's ST doesn't allow third party material is factually wrong about with their options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And again, that doesn't affect me in the slightest; so why would I be annoyed? </div> </div> </div>I don't know. You're the one agreeing the people that use (for whatever reasons) the officially updated Numina for 20th are tiresome. You're the one agreeing that a proper Sorcerer 20th book needs to copy Sorcerer Revised instead of WoD: Sorcerer to create a two-tier Numina user scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This isn't an issue of annoyance or empathy; it's a matter of facts. </div> </div> </div>But it isn't a matter of facts. There is no Sorcerer 20th book. There's a popular homebrew ruleset out there. If I posted a link to my personal HtR 20th edition, even if everyone thought it was awesome, it wouldn't mean there's a H20. If it was just about facts, that would be the end of it.<br /> <br /> The emotional stuff matters because it's clearly fueled the opening post of the thread, and its why you want people to treat S:PoP as if it were an official book, like right here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point here is that they're only \u201cnot getting an S20\u201d if they don't accept S:PoP as a proper S20. </div> </div> </div>Accepting it as a proper S20 is not factual. A proper S20 would be something licensed for full publication by Paradox. S:PoP is a very good non-proper S20; claiming otherwise is denying reality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T07:15:52-08:00","id":1471655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471611#post1471611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think from a canon perspective, there has to be some sort of distinction between the two. There are individuals known as &quot;dabblers&quot; in numina that have been mentioned in various WOD sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>In WoD, I would call a dabbler in medicine someone that mechanically has 1 dot in Medicine, and an expert (or someone who's deeply invested on it as a science and not just a tool) to someone who has 4-5.<i> I would never use the words &quot;dabbbler in X&quot; to define someone who's *not* using X</i>, but something fundamentaly different, with different rules<br /> <br /> And that's the key here: I could use HH2 Paths to represent a Sorcerer that's *not* a &quot;dabbler&quot; by...giving the Sorcerer various Paths, or Paths at lvl 5 instead of 1 or 2 dots, \u00bfhow's that different from not being a &quot;dabbler&quot;, but someone who's focused and wants to expend a lot of time/effort in the arts? - well, your whole point it's that Sorcerers that were defined as &quot;not dabblers&quot; used to have different, stronger, rules. Isn't it?<br /> <br /> Problem is, Sorcerer itself never presented it's rules as anything else but sorcery Paths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We also have to explain what caused sorcery to become more diverse and powerful from the old days of Acensions Right Hand </div> </div> </div>You got me in this first half, yes we do. But then...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> where the magic practices was explicitly stated to be a weaker and inferior power that was not truly magic at all. But by the time of Second editions WOD: Sorcerer, this was changed to the sorcery being real magic just inferior magic and when Sorcerer:Revised was released sorcery just followed a &quot;separate but equal&quot; approach with sorcerers viewed as mages in their own right, just using a different type of magic </div> </div> </div>.<br /> The idea presented in Sorcerer: Revised was that this whole &quot;sorcerers are inferior&quot; was ALWAYS prejudice from mages, not that Sorcery literally shifted into a different form of magic over the ages<br /> <br /> OOC magic rules changed to reflect various interests and concerns. But IOC they were always the same thing, fundamentaly. Sorcerer already did that change you're criticizing, but the other way arround - I don't see what these &quot;ST's&quot; are doing as wrong, because it &quot;makes sense&quot; to think HH2 rules are meant to be used for Sorcerers. Just as old editions had different rules for the same subject.<br /> <br /> A completely different beast it's if they &quot;should&quot; be used that way. If such simplified rules presented in books that *aren't* about Sorcerers are, perhaps, undoing a lot of evolution on the subject. To say S20 it's better, I can see (for that reason and others). To say that what we have in 20th canon isn't meant to be used for sorcerers at all...I can't see that quite as clearly<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is also the lore that states the mindset of people who practice sorcery and that lore does not appear for a mortal in HH II, Kinfolk, or Ghost Hunter. </div> </div> </div>What we lack it's lore to state that such mindset change the way Sorcery works at such a fundamental level, that using rules of books that don't talk about the Yearning should be regarded as an obvious mistake.<br /> <br /> Like, say, to put an example: thinking that Black Hand book it's &quot;updating&quot; M20 core rules in a way that now mages use the altered Pillar &amp; Paradox systems instead of Spheres, just because BH2 comes after M20, would have been quite wrong in my opinion- not just because we have other newer M20 books, but also because the rules were <i>meant</i> to be simplified rules, it was even implied that these mages used Pillars because they were issolated.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, note that some use these rules as &quot;updated&quot; <i>Pillar rules for the modern era,</i> to say mages in the modern era can use Pillar magick, and use those Paradox rules. I wouldn't call *that* a mistake, even if probably a new Mage book about Pillars would have more complex rules...and even when it can be debated<i> how much Pillars and Spheres</i> <i>exist as such IOC</i> (but that's a whole 'nother can of worms)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the context of M20: HH2, Kinfolk, and Ghost Hunter hedge magicians are implicitly Practicing some form of Gutter Magic \u2014 though the HH2 crowd tends to combine this with High Ritual Magic while Kinfolk tend to lean more toward a mix with Shamanism. As Starcomet points out, the flavor text for the Sorcerer books is quite different from the flavor text for most other books featuring Hedge Magic, as the former portrays sorcerers as people who know what they're doing whole the latter portrays hedge magicians as people groping around in the dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, as I pointed out, Asencions Rigth Hand <i>doesn't </i>and has different - weaker - rules. Sorcerer: Revised - same. Arcanum, Starcomet pointed out that they *shouldn't* be people &quot;groping around in the dark&quot;, and yet have those rules<br /> <br /> There's not <i>enough</i> <i>reason </i>to think they're using a different kind of power with different rules just beause they have a different &quot;Focus&quot;. That's not the way &quot;Paradigm&quot; was defined to interact with Sorcery in any book - it changed the tools and rituals employed but Paths stayed the same.<br /> <br /> My point it's that it's not <u><i>evident</i></u> to me, in any way, that they should be using different rules. I can see it as a posibility, but not as fact<br /> <br /> It can be defended as a theory with existing Lore (in a similar way as one can defend, say, different theories about the Umbra), and I could defend that perhaps it <i>should </i>be the case. But I would never, ever, think that people saying: &quot;well, 20th anniv has Paths - let's use those to do sorcerers&quot; are doing something against the intent of the books about what sorcerers *are* in the canon.<br /> <br /> Two different beasts. They're not using house rules against the intent of the canon or the Lore, they're just using a different approach that higligths different consequences and assumptions about those two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-02-2022, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T07:16:08-08:00","id":1471656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471646#post1471646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. So I don't get the argument that a proper Sorcerer 20th is necessary to make psychics and sorcerers that aren't going to fall behind the mages if that was never actually true in a general sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand, just because sorcery is slower and a bit more costly does not mean they will always fall behind. My sorcerer in an M20 game did not certainly fall behind that much and it was only because of his flaw that made him less flexible. However, using the Numina in the three 20th edition books, they will always fall behind given how weak and limited they are compared to the sorcery in Sorcerer: Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T07:48:03-08:00","id":1471657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471655#post1471655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In WoD, I would call a dabbler in Medicine someone that mechanically has 1 dot in medicine, and an expert someone who has 4-5. I would never use the words &quot;dabbbler in X&quot; to define someone who's *not* using X, but something fundamentaly different<br /> <br /> And that's the key here: I could use HH2 Paths to represent a Sorcerer that's *not* a &quot;dabbler&quot; by...giving the Sorcerer various Paths, or Paths at lvl 5, \u00bfhow's that different from not being a &quot;dabbler&quot;, but someone who's focused and wants to expend a lot of time/effort in the arts? - well, your whole point it's that Sorcerers defined as &quot;not dabblers&quot; used to have different, stronger, rules.<br /> <br /> Problem is, Sorcerer itself never presented it's rules as anything else but sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hmm you could argue that, but even the Order of Hermes, with their classification systems, recognizes that there is a dabbler level when it comes to sorcery/hedge magic. They list three types of magic: Goetia, Thuergia, and Magia. Goetia to them is the lowest form of magic and is in their minds no better than parlour tricks. It is rustic, disorganized, and its practioners are implied to be doing things they do not understand. Thuergia is the highest form of sorcery that follows &quot;proper&quot; ritual practices and hermetic principals according to their classication. Finally, Magia is the &quot;true&quot; sphere magick that Mages practices. The first two categories clearly refer to sorcery and even the Order of Hermes, with all of their prejudices, recognize there is a different between someone doing Goetia and someone doing Theurgia.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471655#post1471655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the idea presented in Sorcerer: Revised was that this while &quot;sorcerers are inferior&quot; was ALWAYS prejudice from mages, not that Sorcery literally shifted into a diffewrent form of magick over the ages<br /> <br /> See...you're conflating OOC with IOC. OOC magic rules changed to reflect various interests and concerns. But IOC they were always the same thing, fundamentaly. The problem I have with your reasoning it's that Sorcerer already did that change, but the other way arround - I don't see what these &quot;ST's&quot; are doing as wrong, because it &quot;makes sense&quot; to think HH2 rules are meant to be used for Sorcerers that aren't dabblers as the &quot;new edition&quot; take, in the same way as old edditions had a different takes on the same subject, the new edditions can have it too. It makes as much sense to me as to think they *weren't* meant for that. A completely different beast it's if they &quot;should&quot; be used that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of think it is a mix of both prejudices and sorcery literally changing. Here is an exerpt about &quot;hedge&quot; or &quot;craft&quot; magicians from the Hunters: Spellbinder enemy book:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;So why does the difference between<br /> a Tradition witch and a hedge magician matter? It\u2019s<br /> important for you, the Storyteller, to know what you<br /> get the imbued into.<br /> Craft magicians are essentially low-powered mages.<br /> Their capabilities don\u2019t rely on harnessing the ever-shifting<br /> whorls and eddies of reality\u2019s flow. In fact, they<br /> rarely have more than a bag of tricks at their disposal.<br /> Instead of making a Mercedes conveniently explode,<br /> these magicians tend to pull out Tarot cards or \u201cspirit<br /> bags\u201d and perform what might be considered parlor tricks.<br /> They can read futures (with accuracy), conjure small<br /> items or make other items disappear. They might even<br /> be able to \u201cconvince\u201d someone to do something such as<br /> steal an object, as long as the request doesn\u2019t defy the<br /> subject\u2019s nature. But that\u2019s about it. Their repertoire of<br /> capabilities isn\u2019t extensive, although an advantage to<br /> that \u201cweakness\u201d is that they don\u2019t have to worry about<br /> offending reality with their magic...Their magic ducks just under the cosmic radar.&quot;</i> (pg. 90)<br /> <br /> Also, <i>&quot;Craft magicians...suffer serious limitations<br /> when it comes to spell casting. Their Quintessence<br /> never rises higher than 5. They cannot cast spells rated<br /> higher than 2 in any given art. And, their difficulties to<br /> perform magic are increased by one compared to other<br /> mages\u2019 efforts.&quot;</i> (pg. 101)<br /> <br /> Even in Ascensions Right Hand, there was a mechanical difference that blended into the real world canon of the setting. The sorcery/hedge magic presented in WOD: Sorcerer and Sorcerer: Revised is very different from this first edition view of sorcery. Of course, this could be an instance of WOD being, once again, VERY contradictory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 01-02-2022, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T07:55:37-08:00","id":1471658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471653#post1471653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starcomet's opening post is about being tired of people that treat the official 20th books with Numina in them as the updates to the Numina Paths for the 20th books; I don't see a problem characterizing that as a statement of annoyance.<br /> <br /> You agreed with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I didn't intend to; I only intended to agree with the overall idea of his post. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471653#post1471653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't shift the goal posts. The thread started about complaining about other people in the fandom (again, a post you agreed with), not anyone lamenting the available official options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not shifting goal posts, for two reasons: first, I'm clarifying my actual intent, which was never what you're telling me it was; and second, this discussion isn't a game, where there are victory conditions. <br /> <br /> I will now summarily ignore any argument you make that's based on the premise that I'm annoyed with anyone, because I'm not; and I'm not going to defend a position that I don't hold. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471653#post1471653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please explain what a player who's ST doesn't allow third party material is factually wrong about with their options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Up until now, the discussion has been about gamers, not specifically players. In particular, you've been talking in terms of people who have a choice as to what books to consider using. In that regard, it's entirely reasonable for me to mention another option to them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471653#post1471653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're the one agreeing that a proper Sorcerer 20th book needs to copy Sorcerer Revised instead of WoD: Sorcerer to create a two-tier Numina user scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is that the two-tiered scale <i>exists</i>. It's inherent in the existing published material, with the sorcerer books all describing sorcerers as having a better handle on what they're doing than what the non-sorcerer books describe for their hedge magicians. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471653#post1471653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it isn't a matter of facts. There is no Sorcerer 20th book. There's a popular homebrew ruleset out there. If I posted a link to my personal HtR 20th edition, even if everyone thought it was awesome, it wouldn't mean there's a H20. If it was just about facts, that would be the end of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary: if you were to point out a homebrew HtR20 book that's popular and does everything I want when I'm looking for a HtR book, I'd thank you and then use it. Because to me, the issue isn't whether or not the book is \u201ccanon\u201d; it's about whether the book is useful. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471653#post1471653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The emotional stuff matters because it's clearly fueled the opening post of the thread, and its why you want people to treat S:PoP as if it were an official book, like right here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point here is that they're only \u201cnot getting an S20\u201d if they don't accept S:PoP as a proper S20. </div> </div> </div>Accepting it as a proper S20 is not factual. A proper S20 would be something licensed for full publication by Paradox. S:PoP is a very good non-proper S20; claiming otherwise is denying reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with how you're interpreting \u201cproper\u201d. As I said above: to me, whether or not it has Paradox's stamp of approval takes back seat to whether or not it is well written and lets me run the games I want. If it does the latter, then it's a proper book. That's a personal judgment call to be made by each gamer; and if they decide to reject S:PoP as an option, that's their choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-02-2022, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T08:04:50-08:00","id":1471659,"title":"","content":"Again, I understand why people want to stick to official books and that is fine there is nothing wrong with that. I am not annoyed at people who want to try and remain official. My annoyance is everyone acting like, for sorcerers, there are no alternatives. When even M20 states that you should look to WOD: Sorcerer or Sorcerer: Revised if you want to include sorcerers, I just find it odd everyone wants to toss them aside and use these three books as the new universal standard for sorcery in the WOD instead of just for that specific gameline or setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T08:19:25-08:00","id":1471661,"title":"","content":"This argument makes me scratch my head lol. Or toss my hair and laugh (though I mostly do that when I know something\u2019s supposed to be funny but I\u2019m not sure why). I like Paths of Power and I use it even though I know it\u2019s not official. I also don\u2019t really care if other groups use it or not. So I guess I don\u2019t really get what you guys are arguing about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T08:32:48-08:00","id":1471663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471661#post1471661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This argument makes me scratch my head lol. Or toss my hair and laugh (though I mostly do that when I know something\u2019s supposed to be funny but I\u2019m not sure why). I like Paths of Power and I use it even though I know it\u2019s not official. I also don\u2019t really care if other groups use it or not. So I guess I don\u2019t really get what you guys are arguing about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think now the main argument is whether there is a difference between dabbler sorcery and real sorcery and whether the magic in HH II and others is suppose to be the same sorcery that has appeared in WOD: Sorcerer or Sorcerer: Revised or its own &quot;dabbler&quot; variant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T08:41:57-08:00","id":1471666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471655#post1471655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, as I pointed out, Ascension's Rigth Hand <i>doesn't </i>and has different - weaker - rules. Sorcerer: Revised - same. Arcanum, Starcomet pointed out that they *shouldn't* be people \u201cgroping around in the dark\u201d, and yet have those rules</div> </div> </div> </div>ARH generally doesn't go into any detail on the issue; the closest it gets is a single box about Magical Styles (p.97) that said that, yes, hedge magicians have them. SRev is definitely in the camp of \u201cthese guys know what they're doing\u201d, as is Halls of the Arcanum. [EDIT: actually, not. I just reviewed Halls of the Arcanum; and the book makes the point that those members of the Arcanum that have access to Numina are rare and an extremely eclectic group, with no consistency to their mystical beliefs. In M20 terms, I'd definitely describe them as practicing Gutter Magic, too; they just have a lot more of it than most.] I'd also add World of Darkness: Sorcerer to that list. As for the game systems each presents, I haven't been commenting on that and I'll leave that for others to hash out. My main focus here has been on, well, Focus. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471655#post1471655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not <i>enough</i> <i>reason </i>to think they're using a different kind of power with different rules just beause they have a different &quot;Focus&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed; and I've never argued otherwise. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471655#post1471655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be defended as a theory with existing Lore (in a similar way as one can defend, say, different theories about the Umbra), and I could defend that perhaps it <i>should </i>be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is pretty much what I'm saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-02-2022, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T08:46:51-08:00","id":1471667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471657#post1471657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hmm you could argue that, but even the Order of Hermes, with their classification systems, recognizes that there is a dabbler level when it comes to sorcery/hedge magic. They list three types of magic: Goetia, Thuergia, and Magia. Goetia to them is the lowest form of magic and is in their minds no better than parlour tricks. It is rustic, disorganized, and its practioners are implied to be doing things they do not understand. Thuergia is the highest form of sorcery that follows &quot;proper&quot; ritual practices and hermetic principals according to their classication. Finally, Magia is the &quot;true&quot; sphere magick that Mages practices. The first two categories clearly refer to sorcery and even the Order of Hermes, with all of their prejudices, recognize there is a different between someone doing Goetia and someone doing Theurgia.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The way I've interpreted their magical hierarchy it's that everyone uses High Ritual but not everyone can make it work the same. There's those that were taught Hermetism but can't do much with it (represented by Occult, now Esoterica would be better), those that can apply Sorcery with their teachings, and those that do Magic(k).<br /> <br /> If anything, the &quot;least&quot; users can activate purely &quot;mundane&quot; magic (or magick) - like when demon summoning rituals don't require Paths <i>nor </i>Spheres to use (but you really shouldn't do it, because Paths &amp; Spheres allow you to protect yourself), the next tier uses Paths and the next uses Spheres (one could extrapolate with how normal scientists can use technology, Extraordinary ones use Paths, and then there's the <i>real </i>Technocrat)<br /> <br /> Note: Hermetic Awakened Mages practice the 3 in DA (more close to their real world counterparts, really). But I would say it still applies, Lore wise, just with different names, and maybe could demand different rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I kind of think it is a mix of both prejudices and sorcery literally changing. Here is an exerpt about &quot;hedge&quot; or &quot;craft&quot; magicians from the Hunters: Spellbinder enemy book: </div> </div> </div>What I see there it's that Hunter it's talking about the difference between True Mages and Sorcerers. It just calls them different names because Hunter does that all the time.<br /> <br /> The same way &quot;Spheres&quot; are completely different with different rules and names in Hunter. It's not defining a &quot;third&quot; group of dynamic magic, nor retconning Mage - it's merely re-defining stuff.<br /> <br /> (And it's a perfect example for when a change in the rules it's most obviously &quot;not canon&quot;. Hunter doesn't change Mage rules even when it came after, Because it's <i>explicitly </i>a simplified Antagonist system for Hunter, it says so in the books. It points you towards Ascencion for a more complex take. Now, If Hunter was the only book of a new edition with Mages on it...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even in Ascensions Right Hand, there was a mechanical difference that blended into the real world canon of the setting. </div> </div> </div>What was it?<br /> <br /> My interpretation it's that some Sorcerers get more dots in their sheets to spread arround Paths, and reduced xp costs compared with other games. Personaly, I wouldn't use Sorcerer: Revised or S20 for one type of Sorcerer AND HH2, etc. for the other. I would use one for both. I've never interpreted any rule in any book about <i>Paths being different depending on who uses them.</i><br /> <br /> BUT I'm not saying you're dead wrong about that being the way things are. It's just a different interpretation. I see how a new Sorcerer book could incorporate both systems - a bit complicated for my taste, but could have merit if one wants a harder divide between both &quot;types&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-02-2022, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T09:26:06-08:00","id":1471670,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, feeling like the &quot;intended target&quot; of this post, I'm frankly just glad to see that people whose experience and opinions I respect seem to disagree on this matter, rather than it being a straight-up obvious mistake on my part, haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T09:54:53-08:00","id":1471672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471667#post1471667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I've interpreted their magical hierarchy it's that everyone uses High Ritual but not everyone can make it work the same. There's those that were taught Hermetism but can't do much with it (represented by Occult, now Esoterica would be better), those that can apply Sorcery with their teachings, and those that do Magic(k).<br /> <br /> If anything, the &quot;least&quot; users can activate purely &quot;mundane&quot; magic (or magick) - like when demon summoning rituals don't require Paths <i>nor </i>Spheres to use (but you really shouldn't do it, because Paths &amp; Spheres allow you to protect yourself), the next tier uses Paths and the next uses Spheres (one could extrapolate with how normal scientists can use technology, Extraordinary ones use Paths, and then there's the <i>real </i>Technocrat)<br /> <br /> Note: Hermetic Awakened Mages practice the 3 in DA (more close to their real world counterparts, really). But I would say it still applies, Lore wise, just with different names, and maybe could demand different rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That is an interesting interpretation of it! But one could argue that those who use Goetia are dabblers as they do not fully understand the magick they are working with. The more skilled and knowledable they become, they then begin to practice Theurgia. Hopefully, they will then gain the englightenment needed and practice Magia. But there is no general &quot;mundane&quot; mortal magick that I know of. There is either path based magick or sphere based magick. Anything else is its own category that does not fit within the Goetia framework the OoH has, though demon pacts or infernalism could fit that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471667#post1471667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I see there it's that Hunter it's talking about the difference between True Mages and Sorcerers. It just calls them different names because Hunter does that all the time.<br /> <br /> The same way &quot;Spheres&quot; are completely different with different rules and names in Hunter. It's not defining a &quot;third&quot; group of dynamic magic, nor retconning Mage - it's merely re-defining stuff.<br /> <br /> (And it's a perfect example for when a change in the rules it's most obviously &quot;not canon&quot;. Hunter doesn't change Mage rules even when it came after, Because it's <i>explicitly </i>a simplified Antagonist system for Hunter, it says so in the books. It points you towards Ascencion for a more complex take. Now, If Hunter was the only book of a new edition with Mages on it...)</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right that it is simplified for a Hunter game but since it is still a first edition book it still states that the hedge magicians are weak, inferior, and only know a few bags of tricks from a lore perspective. Sorcery/hedge magic in first edition followed a different mindset compared to what we see in second edition and revised where sorcerers could do much more than tell fortunes or conjure small things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471667#post1471667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was it?<br /> <br /> My interpretation it's that some Sorcerers get more dots in their sheets to spread arround Paths, and reduced xp costs compared with other games. Personaly, I wouldn't use Sorcerer: Revised or S20 for one type of Sorcerer AND HH2, etc. for the other. I would use one for both. I've never interpreted any rule in any book about <i>Paths being different depending on who uses them.</i><br /> <br /> BUT I'm not saying you're dead wrong about that being the way things are. It's just a different interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sadly do not have direct quotes as I read that book months ago and no longer have access to it, but I know reading through it it gave me the impression that hedge magic was not real magic and it was definitely different than what we see in second and revised edition. The paths that have remained the same somewhat since first edition are Cursing and Alchemy, but even these have under gone changes if we include the HH II updates. Cursings went from only dealing with weak curses, to being able to curse and bless for generations in revised and able to kill or stop death, to back to dealing only with curses that have a high cost to the user and can only last a year at most in HH II. Alchemy remained largely consistent with the last 6th dot capable of producing the panacea, philosopher's stone, and awakening. In HH II, there is no sixth dot or mention of the alchemist being able to make the philosopher's stone or awakening.<br /> <br /> For a V20 game where one of the players is a hunter with some sorcery or psychic powers, I would allow only the material that appears in HH II. Same with a kinfolk in a W20 game using only the KF:ABA book. But in a M20 game, using these two books or WOD: GH is a huge disservice to a sorcerer NPC or a player. I can see the appeal, but the magick in those books are of a dabbler sort if you will since a hunter and kinfolk do not have the same skill or mindset as a skilled sorcerer would. Both the M20 core rulebook and Gods and Monsters states that if you wish to include sorcerers in your game it points you to WOD: Sorcerer and Sorcerer: Revised, not HH II or KF: ABA.<br /> <br /> This is not saying the magick is inherently different. It is still sorcery, but users of it are of a dabbler quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 01-02-2022, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T10:02:30-08:00","id":1471673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471666#post1471666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the game systems each presents, I haven't been commenting on that and I'll leave that for others to hash out. My main focus here has been on, well, Focus.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for misinterpreting your intent.<br /> <br /> As a matter of Focus. Focus <i>for mages</i> rarely represents a lessened potential - certainly not the way not having the Yearning does for Sorcerers. Gutter Magick it's a no less valid road for Ascencion, Power or whatever - your magic(k) can be every bit as potent as that of a High Wizard.<br /> <br /> From what was transpiring in the tread, I would read that's <i>not the same</i> for Sorcerers. Practice matters, &quot;not knowing what you're doing&quot; matters. Apparently. Unless I was also misinterpreting that part too. I think there's an idea that needs developping.<br /> <br /> One posibility on a Mage-centric perspective, perhaps Sorcery it's easier on Paradigms that have been generating &quot;mythic threads&quot; for a time. A bit like undercurrents of Reality-warp. Maybe some Practices do have a stronger tie to the Foundations (or other external forces) than others (other kinds of supernatural insigth, like Magick for instance, can have different &quot;vehicles&quot;).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T10:21:20-08:00","id":1471675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471672#post1471672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right that it is simplified for a Hunter game but since it is still a first edition book it still states that the hedge magicians are weak, inferior, and only know a few bags of tricks from a lore perspective. Sorcery/hedge magic in first edition followed a different mindset compared to what we see in second edition and revised where sorcerers could do much more than tell fortunes or conjure small things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter it's all Revised (It's 1e only in the sense that there wasn't another). It also comes, if I'm not mistaken, after most Mage: Revised books.<br /> <br /> However, it's perspective about sorcerers being weaker, inferior, etc...I think it's not a commentary on Mage, but rather than Hunter perspective it's limited. Hunter perspective it's that of &quot;you will kill this people&quot;, and most Sorcerers are exactly what's being described. That is: on the weak end. Even Sorcerer Sorcerers start with only 6 dots (typically in more than one Path), and one or two rituals. That's &quot;a few tricks&quot; from the Awakened perspective. The Yearning doesn't grant you several Paths at 5-6, and uncountable rituals :P . Even among the best of the best it's rare to ever reach such high places.<br /> <br /> It's like how the Werewolf Enemy Book only talks very little about the Spirits. The intention isn't to get in trouble with the Incarna hierarcy, merely to show that the Garou are more than furballs of senseless rage.One needs to treat these books with a grain of salt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T10:39:41-08:00","id":1471676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471675#post1471675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunter it's all Revised (It's 1e only in the sense that there wasn't another). It also comes, if I'm not mistaken, after most Mage: Revised books.<br /> <br /> However, it's perspective about sorcerers being weaker, inferior, etc...I think it's not a commentary on Mage, but rather than Hunter perspective it's limited. Hunter perspective it's that of &quot;you will kill this people&quot;, and most Sorcerers are exactly what's being described. That is: on the weak end. Even Sorcerer Sorcerers start with only 6 dots (typically in more than one Path), and one or two rituals. That's &quot;a few tricks&quot; from the Awakened perspective. The Yearning doesn't grant you several Paths at 5-6, and uncountable rituals :P . Even among the best of the best it's rare to ever reach such high places.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those 6 dots in path and 6 dots in rituals would give a lot more than a few tricks though! You are right that from a Hunter's perspective they are still seen as limited compared to what Mages can do, but the books implies that a Hunter would only ever come across a sorcerer that could perform rank 2 versions of the spheres. We both know full well that sorcerers could produce up to rank 4 or even 5 in some regards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T10:43:59-08:00","id":1471677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sadly do not have direct quotes as I read that book months ago and no longer have access to it, but I know reading through it it gave me the impression that hedge magic was not real magic and it was definitely different than what we see in second and revised edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well. My point was that this perspective changing shows that different rules can represent the same Sorcery. These were, as some say, OOC changes. There was an <i>authorial desicion</i> to make Mage 2e and 1e perspectives to be factualy wrong - and not like they're &quot;different sorcerers&quot;, but more like: Mages are too proud of themselves, and confirmation bias often proves them rigth - so.<br /> <br /> There was a retcon (several of them): That's for certain. The thing is, not having a better canonical source for 20th era, one could always think there was <i>another </i>retcon. And if that's a disservice or not...well, it's a bit subjective. For instance, I never like Alchemy granting Paradox-free inmortality in Mage games (given how much of a big deal Mage makes of inmortality) - I wouldn't be peeved if they removed that. But it looks like you <i>want </i>Alchemists to become inmortal in a reliable way. So...<br /> <br /> But I get it: There was a movement to make Sorcerers into more than second rate citizens of Mage: the Ascencion, like some sort of &quot;ghouls for mages&quot;. M20 <i>doesn't seem to be against this</i>: It <i>deliberately</i> left Sorcerers out because they were too complex and their own thing (then there's the simplified rules in Gods and Monsters - but that's not meant for PC), so it may feel a little invasive when someone want's to grab a Vampire book to rule Sorcerers in a way you feel it steals the thunder from them. I think a case could be made to say that there is no canon for Sorcerer in M20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T10:52:28-08:00","id":1471678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471676#post1471676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those 6 dots in path and 6 dots in rituals would give a lot more than a few tricks though! You are right that from a Hunter's perspective they are still seen as limited compared to what Mages can do, but the books implies that a Hunter would only ever come across a sorcerer that could perform rank 2 versions of the spheres. We both know full well that sorcerers could produce up to rank 4 or even 5 in some regards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Hunter Spheres aren't exactly the same, they do offer a little more punch at some levels. Still, you're likely correct in that some powers even a young Sorcerer would have access to, may be hard to replicate under those conditions ... better don't think to much about it<br /> <br /> Elder vampires can make infinite actions per turn in Hunter's core. And Demons can create other splats, including Werewolves and Mages, in their Enemy book (and it's suggested that may have created the supernatural - yet mages can make Demons in *their* Hunter books. So, what came first the demon or the mage? :P ), Hunter Enemy books are interesting but weird. It's a very, very, limited perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T11:25:15-08:00","id":1471680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471678#post1471678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that Hunter Spheres aren't exactly the same, they do offer a little more punch at some levels. Still, you're likely correct in that some powers even a young Sorcerer would have access to, may be hard to replicate under those conditions ... better don't think to much about it<br /> <br /> Elder vampires can make infinite actions per turn in Hunter's core. And Demons can create other splats, including Werewolves and Mages, in their Enemy book (and it's suggested that may have created the supernatural - yet mages can make Demons in *their* Hunter books. So, what came first the demon or the mage? :P ), Hunter Enemy books are interesting but weird. It's a very, very, limited perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed, and I see it as an example of WOD infamous contradictions when it comes to cross splat interactions. It is similar to how Demons are immune to all mind effects in the Demon games, but in Mage and Sorcerer it states you can mentally compel demons to obey you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T11:28:38-08:00","id":1471681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471677#post1471677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a case could be made to say that there is no canon for Sorcerer in M20</div> </div> </div> </div>You are a right, there is a good case that be made that no canon exists for Sorcerers currently in M20. They still exists and we know some things, but any further details is just speculation at this point and up to players to decide.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T13:37:15-08:00","id":1471687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471673#post1471673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for misinterpreting your intent.<br /> <br /> As a matter of Focus. Focus <i>for mages</i> rarely represents a lessened potential - certainly not the way not having the Yearning does for Sorcerers. Gutter Magick it's a no less valid road for Ascension, Power or whatever - your magic(k) can be every bit as potent as that of a High Wizard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Practitioners of Gutter Magic are looked down upon by practitioners of more defined arts; Gutter Magic is basically the M20 replacement for \u201cyou don't have a paradigm, and make do with whatever scraps you manage to find\u201d. Basically, the earlier editions' Orphans. Likewise, the Hedge Magic of HH2, Kinfolk, and GH are all described in terms along the lines of not having a cohesive worldview and foraging for scraps. <br /> <br /> In terms of things like the Yearning or being initiated into the Otherworld, that's not really a thing in terms of game systems; it's part of the fluff about how sorcerers take the art seriously, and invest more into it than the dabblers in Hedge Magic such as hunters and Kinfolk. The only way that sorcerers are more powerful than hedge magicians in terms of game mechanics is that they're given an initial allotment of Paths, whereas the various hedge magicians have to buy their Paths with freebie points. So for the most part, the distinction between sorcerer and hedge magician is very similar to the distinction between mage and Orphan. <br /> <br /> S:PoP also has a section on \u201cMaking Sorcerers More Powerful\u201d for use by Storytellers who don't want the sorcerers falling too far behind. There's not much to it (in a nutshell, \u201cremove fast-casting penalty if you want faster sorcerers; remove the penalty for witnesses if you want sorcerers to be able to cast more freely; and only require the highest Aspect of a casting if you want sorcerers to be more powerful\u201d); but the point is that there <i>are</i> tweaks that can be made to buff sorcerers if the Storyteller feels they need buffing; and if you want a mechanical distinction between the dabblers in Hedge Magic and the professional sorcerers, you can say that once a mortal has been initiated into sorcery, she gains access to the sorcery buffs. <br /> <br /> That said, I've been using \u201cdabbler\u201d not in the sense of \u201conly has one or two dots\u201d, but rather in the sense of \u201cHedge Magic isn't what the character is primarily about\u201d. A vampire hunter is primarily about hunting vampires; he may learn a bit of Hedge Magic to that end. But even if he's invested five dots in, say, Divination, he's still a vampire hunter first and a Diviner second. Whereas a sorcerer who hunts vampires is a sorcerer first and foremost and a vampire hunter secondarily. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> On the digression to HtR: the Enemy Books were designed with a \u201cthere are more thing in heaven and on earth than are dreamt of in your philosophy\u201d mindset: the vampires in The Nocturnal aren't necessarily the Kindred of VtM; the werewolves in The Moonstruck aren't necessarily the Garou of WtA; and the witches in The Spellbound aren't necessarily the Awakened of MtAs <i>or</i> the sorcerers of, well, Sorcerer. The idea in all cases wasn't just that they were presenting a stripped down version of the other gamelines, but also that they were open enough in their design that you could confound the players who were well versed in the associated game by having your monster do things that you wouldn't see happen in the other game. <br /> <br /> As such, I do <i>not</i> consider Hunter's Enemy books to be a valid source of information about the games that inspired them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-03-2022, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T21:07:19-08:00","id":1471714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471687#post1471687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practitioners of Gutter Magic are looked down upon by practitioners of more defined arts; Gutter Magic is basically the M20 replacement for \u201cyou don't have a paradigm, and make do with whatever scraps you manage to find. Basically, the earlier editions' Orphans. Likewise, the Hedge Magic of HH2, Kinfolk, and GH are all described in terms along the lines of not having a cohesive worldview and foraging for scraps. <br /> <br /> In terms of things like the Yearning or being initiated into the Otherworld, that's not really a thing in terms of game systems; it's part of the fluff about how sorcerers take the art seriously, and invest more into it than the dabblers in Hedge Magic such as hunters and Kinfolk. The only way that sorcerers are more powerful than hedge magicians in terms of game mechanics is that they're given an initial allotment of Paths, whereas the various hedge magicians have to buy their Paths with freebie points. So for the most part, the distinction between sorcerer and hedge magician is very similar to the distinction between mage and Orphan. <br /> <br /> S:PoP also has a section on \u201cMaking Sorcerers More Powerful\u201d for use by Storytellers who don't want the sorcerers falling too far behind. There's not much to it (in a nutshell, \u201cremove fast-casting penalty if you want faster sorcerers; remove the penalty for witnesses if you want sorcerers to be able to cast more freely; and only require the highest Aspect of a casting if you want sorcerers to be more powerful\u201d); but the point is that there <i>are</i> tweaks that can be made to buff sorcerers if the Storyteller feels they need buffing; and if you want a mechanical distinction between the dabblers in Hedge Magic and the professional sorcerers, you can say that once a mortal has been initiated into sorcery, she gains access to the sorcery buffs. <br /> <br /> That said, I've been using \u201cdabbler\u201d not in the sense of \u201conly had one or two dots\u201d, but rather in the sense of \u201cHedge Magic isn't what the character is primarily about\u201d. A vampire hunter is primarily about hunting vampires; he may learn a bit of Hedge Magic to that end. But even if he's invested five dots in, say, Divination, he's still a vampire hunter first and a Diviner second. Whereas a sorcerer who hunts vampires is a sorcerer first and foremost and a vampire hunter secondarily. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> On the digression to HtR: the Enemy Books were designed with a \u201cthere are more thing in heaven and on earth than are dreamt of in your philosophy\u201d mindset: the vampires in The Nocturnal aren't necessarily the Kindred of VtM; the werewolves in The Moonstruck aren't necessarily the Garou of WtA; and the witches in The Spellbound aren't necessarily the Awakened of MtAs <i>or</i> the sorcerers of, well, Sorcerer. The idea in all cases wasn't just that they were presenting a stripped down version of the other gamelines, but also that they were open enough in their design that you could confound the players who were well versed in the associated game by having your monster do things that you wouldn't see happen in the other game. <br /> <br /> As such, I do <i>not</i> consider Hunter's Enemy books to be a valid source of information about the games that inspired them.</div> </div> </div> </div>After thinking about this carefully, I agree. There is a qualitative distinction between hunters and Kinfolk who dabble in hedge magic and \u201ctrue\u201d sorcerers. Plus reading this discussion inspired me to go back and reread my copy of Paths of Power. So thanks \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T06:07:09-08:00","id":1471774,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471687#post1471687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practitioners of Gutter Magic are looked down upon by practitioners of more defined arts; Gutter Magic is basically the M20 replacement for \u201cyou don't have a paradigm, and make do with whatever scraps you manage to find\u201d. Basically, the earlier editions' Orphans. Likewise, the Hedge Magic of HH2, Kinfolk, and GH are all described in terms along the lines of not having a cohesive worldview and foraging for scraps.<br /> <br /> In terms of things like the Yearning or being initiated into the Otherworld, that's not really a thing in terms of game systems; it's part of the fluff about how sorcerers take the art seriously, and invest more into it than the dabblers in Hedge Magic such as hunters and Kinfolk. The only way that sorcerers are more powerful than hedge magicians in terms of game mechanics is that they're given an initial allotment of Paths, whereas the various hedge magicians have to buy their Paths with freebie points. So for the most part, the distinction between sorcerer and hedge magician is very similar to the distinction between mage and Orphan.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 stance about Orphans it's that they're not a different type of mage, the distinction it's <i>social </i>in nature. Orphans can be as powerful and driven as institutionalized mages, so much so that there's not even a distinction in the amount of Spheres you get from character generation (even when one could think that being part of an Institution dedicate to magick would allow someone easier access to magical learning - thus Spheres). <br /> <br /> OOC, the point of Orphans it's that they're <i>not</i> qualitatively different from other mages. They don't lack anything but resources, that come with obligations (that some Orphans would call shackles). <br /> <br /> As far as I know, Gutter Mages are, likewise, not inferior in any way. Except some could be Hollow Ones, wich would give them access to some of the advantages of more formal groups that an Orphan with more formal practice BUT no access to the Factions would lack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I've been using \u201cdabbler\u201d not in the sense of \u201conly has one or two dots\u201d, but rather in the sense of \u201cHedge Magic isn't what the character is primarily about\u201d. A vampire hunter is primarily about hunting vampires; he may learn a bit of Hedge Magic to that end. But even if he's invested five dots in, say, Divination, he's still a vampire hunter first and a Diviner second. Whereas a sorcerer who hunts vampires is a sorcerer first and foremost and a vampire hunter secondarily. </div> </div> </div>If the difference between the two &quot;types&quot; it's that some have a lack of interest, or lack of a social aparathus teaching them magic, then I don't see what's the problem with representing *that* with HH2 or any other 20th book. Nor I see how HH2 it's representing that, and not &quot;real&quot; sorcerers with their &quot;new&quot; system<br /> <br /> A doctor that had the best education in the best universities and has the resources of a 1rst world hospital, and a 3rd world doctor that hadn't such a privileged education or resources would work different. But I don't think one should represent that by making Medicine rules for each. It's rather, a matter of Backgrounds, Difficuly, and <i>maybe </i>dots in the skill.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, a character that has spend less time &amp; effort studying Medicine shouldn't be represented with different rules from someone who spended more time &amp; effort. One simply would have less dots than the other (and, likely, more in other areas). <br /> <br /> So: Is a &quot;dabbler&quot; it's a different &quot;type&quot; of sorcerer? , or it's a different type of motivation?. I think these are important questions. These aren't the same thing, and I don't think shouldn be represented the same way<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> S:PoP also has a section on \u201cMaking Sorcerers More Powerful\u201d for use by Storytellers who don't want the sorcerers falling too far behind. There's not much to it (in a nutshell, \u201cremove fast-casting penalty if you want faster sorcerers; remove the penalty for witnesses if you want sorcerers to be able to cast more freely; and only require the highest Aspect of a casting if you want sorcerers to be more powerful\u201d); but the point is that there <i>are</i> tweaks that can be made to buff sorcerers if the Storyteller feels they need buffing; and if you want a mechanical distinction between the dabblers in Hedge Magic and the professional sorcerers, you can say that once a mortal has been initiated into sorcery, she gains access to the sorcery buffs. </div> </div> </div>That would be a less complex system than to utilize two different systems from two different editions <i>if one wants to mark a clear divide between two types of sorcerer</i> (that maybe don't even exist - just like Orphans aren't a &quot;different type&quot; of Mage, but a derogatory Factions use).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T08:46:57-08:00","id":1471780,"title":"","content":"To me, the mechanical reason to prefer S:PoP over HHII+K:ABA+GH is that it's more comprehensive and more consistent. More comprehensive: there are Paths in S:PoP that don't have counterparts in any of the officially published X20 books, but <i>do</i> appear in previous editions of Sorcerer. Using the official X20 supplements doesn't fill these holes. More consistent: compare the Path of Divination as it appears in HHII, K:ABA, and GH. 'Nuff said. <br /> <br /> What's happening here is that the Hedge Magic rules in X20 have been tailored for each gameline. HHII hedge magic was written with vampire hunters in mind; K:ABA hedge magic was written with kinfolk in mind; and GH hedge magic was written with ghost hunters in mind. They were <i>not</i> written with a common framework, as was the case of the original \u201cYear of the Hunter\u201d supplements that mostly riffed off of and added Paths to what was found in Ascension's Right Hand. <br /> <br /> And that lack of consistency in the X20 lines is not an oversight or a mistake. During the KS for GH, I asked about the Path of Divination being classified as a Psychic Phenomenon instead of a Hedge Path, and was told that that was a deliberate design choice. <br /> <br /> That's why I don't consider the Hedge Magic systems presented in HHII, K:ABA, and GH to be parts of a single Hedge Magic system, but rather three separate magic systems that have overlapping terminology. S:PoP doesn't \u201ccorrect\u201d this; it couldn't even if it wanted to. Instead, it presents sorcerers as Hedge Magic through the lens of Mage in exactly the same way that HHII presents Hedge Magic through the lens of Vampire and K:ABA presents Hedge Magic through the lens of Werewolf (and, despite official statements about it being a general WoD supplement, GH presents Hedge Magic through the lens of Wraith). <br /> <br /> The thing is, \u201cthe lens of Mage\u201d is one that puts Focus front and center, allowing you to present sorcerers with wildly different Practices; whereas HHII and K:ABA each focus primarily on what their respective hedge magicians can do and mostly don't bother dealing with how they go about doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T09:34:00-08:00","id":1471782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471780#post1471780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, \u201cthe lens of Mage\u201d is one that puts Focus front and center, allowing you to present sorcerers with wildly different Practices; whereas HHII and K:ABA each focus primarily on what their respective hedge magicians can do and mostly don't bother dealing with how they go about doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know in HH II the only reason given for how said mortal does hedge magic is because of their belief in folk tales, old wives tales, and superstitions. It states if someone does not have this superstitious worldview, then they cannot use hedge magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T10:48:27-08:00","id":1471786,"title":"","content":"Sorcery needs a source book that makes multiple paths clear TO THE STORYTELLER. The various Sorcery books cover one set of ideas. Kinfolk covered a narrow cluster of shamans. Ghouls are functionality closer to D&amp;D Warlocks, as are those Sorcerers using holy numina like the sorcerers depicted in the first edition version of the Society of Leopold. Psionics are also an important style of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> We need guidelines on flavoring Sorcery and Sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T15:30:41-08:00","id":1471804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471780#post1471780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the mechanical reason to prefer S:PoP over HHII+K:ABA+GH is that it's more comprehensive and more consistent. More comprehensive: there are Paths in S:PoP that don't have counterparts in any of the officially published X20 books, but <i>do</i> appear in previous editions of Sorcerer. Using the official X20 supplements doesn't fill these holes. More consistent: compare the Path of Divination as it appears in HHII, K:ABA, and GH. 'Nuff said. <br /> <br /> What's happening here is that the Hedge Magic rules in X20 have been tailored for each gameline. HHII hedge magic was written with vampire hunters in mind; K:ABA hedge magic was written with kinfolk in mind; and GH hedge magic was written with ghost hunters in mind. They were <i>not</i> written with a common framework, as was the case of the original \u201cYear of the Hunter\u201d supplements that mostly riffed off of and added Paths to what was found in Ascension's Right Hand. <br /> <br /> And that lack of consistency in the X20 lines is not an oversight or a mistake. During the KS for GH, I asked about the Path of Divination being classified as a Psychic Phenomenon instead of a Hedge Path, and was told that that was a deliberate design choice. <br /> <br /> That's why I don't consider the Hedge Magic systems presented in HHII, K:ABA, and GH to be parts of a single Hedge Magic system, but rather three separate magic systems that have overlapping terminology. S:PoP doesn't \u201ccorrect\u201d this; it couldn't even if it wanted to. Instead, it presents sorcerers as Hedge Magic through the lens of Mage in exactly the same way that HHII presents Hedge Magic through the lens of Vampire and K:ABA presents Hedge Magic through the lens of Werewolf (and, despite official statements about it being a general WoD supplement, GH presents Hedge Magic through the lens of Wraith). <br /> <br /> The thing is, \u201cthe lens of Mage\u201d is one that puts Focus front and center, allowing you to present sorcerers with wildly different Practices; whereas HHII and K:ABA each focus primarily on what their respective hedge magicians can do and mostly don't bother dealing with how they go about doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You raise a very good point. Different groups can perceive hedge magic in different ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T17:59:08-08:00","id":1471814,"title":"","content":"Honestly kind of agree with the Original poster's assertion that the sources described should not be used as a formal S20 update.<br /> <br /> I disagree that Sorcerer: paths of power is a good alternative though. Spop reverently sticks with the &quot;sorcerers are to mages what ghouls are to vampires&quot; theme sorcerer revised invented, going so far as to make it so that mages are better at making sorcerer paths than Sorcerers are.<br /> <br /> It also fully embraces many of the nerfs WOD20 has for paths in non-sorcerer-centric books. Path of alchemy for example has many of the nerfs found in the HH2 version. In revised edition, the 5th level power in path of alchemy brought it in line with mummy and possessed, in that the maximum of a stat that a human could have with magic was 8(via possession, mummy magic, or copying powers via sorcerer alchemy) and that getting to the 9-10 range requires either becoming a full splat or infernal pacts. HH2 made sorcerers no longer in line with this and I find it strange that Spop embraces this.<br /> <br /> Spop also limits the ability for psychics to learn each sorcerer disciplines. It originally took 14 xp to learn a cross discipline power at first level to represent the effort it to one to learn something outside their comfort zone, but from then on all powers were their norm XP cost. In Spop the initial cost is removed, but psychics are barred from Ever learning rituals or paths that require rituals, Forever. The system just straight up punishes you for being psychic.<br /> <br /> The new paths listed in the book also don't seem to fit. Saturnal anima/saturnal manes stick out for just how specific they are and the fact that, unlike how they portray sorcerer paths, they only have 1 effect line each. I had to take multiple looks to makes sure that they were indeed their own individual sorcerer paths and not part of something else. I've also noticed they've done similar with other paths that used to have more effect variables in previous editions, which makes the &quot;variable effect&quot; system of Sorcerer: Revised that they copies whole-sale rather redundant or entirely nonfunctional depending on how you look at it.<br /> <br /> All in all, I don't recommend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 01-04-2022, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T18:03:52-08:00","id":1471815,"title":"","content":"It has its flaws, yes. But in terms of what options are available, could you recommend a better option?<br /> <br /> Oh: and for what it's worth, the Saturnal Paths aren't new. They appeared in roughly the same form in W20's Wyld West Expansion Pack. All that S:PoP did was to provide a possible explanation for why they're still around (see the entry for the Enlightened Society of the Weeping Moon) and to reprint the Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-05-2022, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T18:12:38-08:00","id":1471816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471815#post1471815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has its flaws, yes. But in terms of what options are available, could you recommend a better option?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any one book? No.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I'd recommend anyone running sorcerer make their own tweaks to the system or make their own entirely. There just aren't any books that do the idea justice.<br /> <br /> My judgement on Spop though is that it costs money to buy and doesn't do enough vs Sorcerer: revised to be worth the price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T20:24:52-08:00","id":1471822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1471598-hunters-hunted-ii-kinfolk-and-ghost-hunters-are-not-sorcerer-20?p=1471816#post1471816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Any one book? No.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I'd recommend anyone running sorcerer make their own tweaks to the system or make their own entirely. There just aren't any books that do the idea justice.<br /> <br /> My judgement on Spop though is that it costs money to buy and doesn't do enough vs Sorcerer: revised to be worth the price.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I played a sorcerer in a M20 game and ran my own WOD discord server, we used a mix of Sorcerer: Revsied, Paths of Power, and Companion with our own tweaks. Willpower costs was removed to make sorcery faster and because willpower was suppose to be a hard to get back resource that required you to roleplay your Nature. Also got rid of Paths of Power's requirement to prepare alchemical reagents weeks in advance before making potions to again speed things up. This turned out quite well and did not cause any issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}